"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"missing_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Correct the Context/Plan premise: the canonical import parser help (build_import in _parsers/core/io.py) currently has only a one-line description and no epilog — specify that the batching/deferred-push narrative must be ADDED as a new parser epilog (the stale 'future batching'/duplicate text lives in docs/import-export.md, not the CLI help).","cohort":["E4"],"criteria":["E4"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.2444,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/core/io.py L45-55: build_import sets description='Import tickets from export NDJSON (clean rebar->rebar migration).' and adds only --dry-run and file; no epilog is passed.","src/rebar/_cli/help/import.txt (full file): 3 lines of body, no mention of 'duplicate' or 'batching' or 'push'.","search_files for 'duplicate' under src/rebar/_cli/help matched only link/overview relation lists, not import help.","docs/import-export.md L79-83 is where 'no batch-commit primitive' / 'deferred to a follow-up task' actually lives — handled by a separate plan bullet ('Correct docs/import-export.md').","src/rebar/_cli/_parser.py L183/204/217/234: build_argument_parser accepts an epilog, but build_import does not use it, so the parser has no narrative help surface to 'update' today."],"finding":"The Context premise 'Import help still describes duplicate creation and future batching' is refuted for the canonical parser help: build_import (src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/core/io.py L45-55) supplies only a one-line description and no epilog, and the packaged artifact src/rebar/_cli/help/import.txt derived from it mentions neither duplicates nor future batching. The stale text is in docs/import-export.md, not the CLI help.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f064e5fa255ae512d","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Context: 'Import help still describes duplicate creation and future batching'; Plan bullet 'Update canonical import parser help before generated artifacts'; ACs 'Canonical import help describes current batching behavior' / 'describes deferred-push behavior' / 'Overview help carries the canonical import summary'","norm_id":"n1cca90cb4c88110a","priority":0.5556,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Executor opens the canonical import parser to 'update' duplicate/batching text and finds none, then must decide whether to ADD an epilog (unscoped) or whether the intended edit belongs only to docs/import-export.md.","gen_cli_help.py --check / overview-summary ACs pass trivially because the one-line description is unchanged, leaving the batching/deferred-push narrative absent from the canonical help while ACs are marked done."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Reword the Context to say the stale batching/duplicate text is in docs/import-export.md, and add an explicit Plan step to give build_import an epilog carrying the current batching + deferred-push summary so gen_cli_help/gen_cli_reference surface it into import.txt, overview.txt, and the CLI reference.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5556,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Name the specific anchor phrases (e.g. '256-event', 'deferred push', 'no whole-file atomicity', 'concurrent import') the focused assertions must match, so each content-presence criterion has a deterministic pass condition.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["F1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.3187,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan bullet: 'Add focused behavioral assertions for generated help and recovery guidance' does not enumerate the exact strings/anchors","ACs are content-presence claims whose observable outcome depends on what the added assertions actually match"],"finding":"Content-presence acceptance criteria ('describes current batching behavior', 'describes deferred-push behavior', 'describes partial results', 'Concurrent-import limitations are explicit') rely on the focused assertions but the plan does not state the specific anchor phrases those assertions must check, so measurability rests on unspecified test internals.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f0ad2284fce7e0c7f","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria: 'Canonical import help describes current batching behavior', 'describes deferred-push behavior', 'User guidance describes partial results', 'Concurrent-import limitations are explicit'","norm_id":"n71f59979e14a3feb","priority":0.4813,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An executor writes a loose substring assertion that passes without the help text actually conveying the 256-event batching or deferred-push behavior"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify, per surface, exactly what the import parser help carries (batching + deferred-push in `description`/`epilog`) versus what docs/import-export.md carries (partial-results, no-atomicity, no-auto-completion, concurrent-duplicate guidance), and confirm the intended overview one-liner is the first `description` line the generator will derive.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.532,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["scripts/gen_cli_help.py `_summary()` derives the overview one-liner from `description.splitlines()[0]` only; `render_route()`/`format_help()` renders the full description (and epilog) into import.txt","Current src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/core/io.py `build_import` has a single-line description and no epilog; import.txt is 9 lines","Plan does not state whether batching/deferred-push text goes in the parser description vs epilog, nor which recovery/limitation guidance is parser-help vs docs/import-export.md"],"finding":"The plan under-specifies WHERE the new import narrative lives across the two surfaces the generators derive from, and how multi-line parser help interacts with the overview one-liner derivation. gen_cli_help.py builds the overview summary from only the FIRST non-blank line of the parser's `description` (`_summary()` -> `description.splitlines()[0]`), while the full import.txt artifact renders the whole `description` (and epilog) via `parser.format_help()`. The plan requires the canonical import help to describe batching + deferred-push AND the overview to carry the summary AND detailed recovery/limitation guidance (partial results, no whole-file atomicity, no auto-completion of partial tickets, concurrent-duplicate risk) — but does not say which of that lands in the parser `description`, a new `epilog`, or docs/import-export.md. An implementer could put a multi-paragraph description (producing an odd/overlong overview one-liner) or cram recovery narrative into argparse help (awkward --help), when the natural home for the crash/atomicity/concurrency narrative is docs/import-export.md.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fbadaad74a05369fe","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan section (steps 1-3, 5-7) and Acceptance Criteria (\"Canonical import help describes...\", \"Overview help carries the canonical import summary\", \"User guidance describes partial results\", \"Guidance promises no whole-file atomicity\")","norm_id":"n6755d470a5eb485f","priority":0.268,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Author places a multi-paragraph description in build_import; overview.txt one-liner for `import` becomes the first paragraph line only, possibly overlong or truncating the intended summary","Author packs crash/atomicity/concurrency narrative into argparse help, producing verbose/awkward `rebar import --help` output when that guidance belongs in docs/import-export.md"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"State that the batching + deferred-push summary goes in the `build_import` parser `description` (first line = the intended overview one-liner) with any longer parser-help detail in an argparse `epilog`, and that the crash/atomicity/concurrency and serial-rerun recovery narrative lives in docs/import-export.md — so `gen_cli_help.py --check` (overview derived from `description.splitlines()[0]`) and the import.txt artifact stay coherent.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v5","material_fingerprint":"2bd1837625bd2d65","material_parts":{"children":["647ea2107ca5072f",0],"description":["3bc382fb3edd7403",2626],"description_boxes":["38efaf2b16858416",0],"file_impact":["8aad2